I have the same issue with beta.2 with following code:

``` js
let id;

function foo() {
    if (typeof id !== 'undefined') {
        return;
    }
    id = setInterval(() => {
        // some stuff
    }, 250);
}

foo();
```

Does the fix affect to my code too?

issue.body:
Version 2.0.0.beta.2 also checked with latest master https://github.com/eslint/eslint/commit/6433b7b4372468d3470d32f6c2285fa9f06e24fa.
Code is:

``` js
let id;

function foo() {
    if (typeof id !== 'undefined') {
        return;
    }
    id = setInterval(() => {
        // some stuff
    }, 250);
}

foo();
```

The output is `1:5  error  'id' is never modified, use 'const' instead  prefer-const`.
But `id` is modified and declaration with `let` shouldn't alert error in this case.
(moved from #5024 as it is not the same)
